      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "The extra point determines the vertical stretch/reflection a.",
        "reasoning": [
          "Substitute the vertex into $y=a(x-h)^2+k$, then use $({{x2}},{{y2}})$ to solve ${{y2}}={{a}}({{offset}})^2{{k|signed}}$.",
          "The resulting coefficient is a={{a}}, so the complete model is $y={{a}}(x{{nh|signed}})^2{{k|signed}}$."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Do not stop after solving for a; put a back into the full vertex-form equation."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
